      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I believe the problem here is that the property ID is not fixed and might vary between each instance of the game, so you want to get the ID at runtime instead. In order to get the property ID since the regular Shader.PropertyToID isn't exposed, you need to use VRCShader.PropertyToID. \n\nVRCShader.PropertyToID only needs the \"_Udon\" prefix for global variables, but for regular uniforms that aren't global it can be used without that prefix. If you check the code for AudioLink, we actually do make use of cached property IDs there as well.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "65e5061def408fcad34fe1f9",
      "aiGenerated": false,
