      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Property ID mappings are not deterministic between different executions of the client so they can't be reliably serialized in editor and reused at runtime. You can you generate mappings at runtime or use property names directly with MaterialPropertyBlock.\n\nFrom the Unity documentation for Shader.PropertyToID:\n\n\"Each name of shader property is assigned an unique integer number in Unity, that stays the same for the whole game. The numbers will not be the same between different runs of the game or between machines, so do not store them or send them over network.\"",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-02-22T20:52:21.961Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "A U# script to feed SpeedTree property blocks to tree meshes generated with Broccoli works fine in the Unity editor preview, but fails in the actual game.  Demo'd with a simple test shader on some of the leaves that only shows the value of (_ST_WindGlobal.x%1) - it cycles from black to white as expected in Unity, but fails ingame despite debug logs showing that the property block values are changing.\n\nAfter further digging, I've determined the root cause of the problem to be that Shader.PropertyToID is inconsistent between the current Editor version & live VRChat; you can grab the IDs by hand with an Editor script and they'll work fine when fed to Udon in the simulation, but the IDs aren't consistent with full VRChat.  This could be resolved with Udon support for the function.",
